(I ran three SQL queries against the sample records. The join returned two rows and included ava@example.test with MUG-001. For the index comparison, I used 20,000 performance rows and compared execution plans to show the impact of indexing.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(This exercise highlighted the value of efficient joins, selective filters, and query planning when working with larger datasets.) Tj
0 -28 Td
/F1 14 Tf
(Portfolio 3: Transactions and Concurrency) Tj
0 -22 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(For this task, I used a temporary counter on orders to test COMMIT, ROLLBACK, and READ COMMITTED isolation. The uncommitted update remained hidden from the other session until it was committed or rolled back.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(The exercise reinforced how transaction boundaries protect consistency while still allowing controlled concurrent access.) Tj
0 -28 Td
/F1 14 Tf
(Portfolio 4: NoSQL and Advanced Data Models) Tj
0 -22 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(I used order_events as the event-document collection. MongoDB inserted four sample events and returned the expected results for four queries. Validation rejected invalid dates and duplicate event IDs.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(This demonstrated how document-based models support flexible event storage while maintaining validation rules.) Tj
0 -28 Td
