(Individual reflection) Tj
0 -22 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(I organized the project database by keeping customers, products, orders, and order items in separate tables. This made the data easier to maintain and reduced duplication.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(I also experienced a two-session concurrency issue where both sessions read the same data before either updated it. This showed the importance of transaction and isolation understanding.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(Additionally, checking the execution plan alongside the results taught me that different database strategies can produce the same output with very different levels of performance.) Tj
